-- `.0.1` chained tuple projection — regression coverage for the Float32
-- lexer work: `0.1` here is lexically identical to an unsuffixed decimal
-- literal at the point the lexer sees the second `.`, so this only stays
-- Int/Dot/Int/Dot/Int (not a broken float-shaped token) because `scan_number`
-- backtracks to a plain integer whenever there's no `f` suffix.
main : -> Int
main() = ((1, 2), (3, 4)).0.1
